# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# This file is a SAFETY CONTROL, not housekeeping.
#
# The working tree contains the author's play data, their own homebrew, and
# text extracted from copyrighted playtest PDFs. None of it may reach a public
# repository. Before publishing, run:
#
#     git ls-files | findstr /i "character event extracted homebrew"
#
# and expect no output.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- personal play data ----------------------------------------------------
data/characters/
data/campaigns/
data/npcs/
data/shops/
data/events.jsonl
# The fight currently on the table: whose turn it is, who is hurt, and every
# monster's hit points. Live play state, not something to publish.
data/encounters/
# The campaign's world map images - personal play data like the rest.
data/maps/
# Who is at the table, and every join token. Ending a session deletes it;
# it must never reach a commit.
data/table.json
data/_table_test.json
data/events-*.jsonl

# --- the user's own homebrew: theirs, not ours to publish -------------------
data/homebrew/
data/homebrew-variants/

# --- anything extracted from a source document -----------------------------
# May contain copyrighted text (Unearthed Arcana, commercial PDFs). The
# extractor ships; its output does not.
library/extracted/
data/extracted/

# --- the shelf: the user's source PDFs, organised --------------------------
# Whole commercial books live here. *.pdf is not globally ignored, so this
# folder is - a shelved Monster Manual must never be one `git add -A` away
# from a public repo.
library/shelf/

# --- whatever the user dropped in --------------------------------------------
inbox/*
!inbox/README.txt

# --- reference corpus: fetched on demand, not redistributed -----------------
# The corpus TEXT is a local fixture and stays out of the repo. The measured
# VECTORS built from it do ship (see below), because without them a fresh
# clone has no "plays most like" at all.
library/corpus/
data/corpus/
library/_manifest.json

# _vectors.json is DELIBERATELY tracked. It holds no rules text - only each
# subclass's name, class, source document and four simulated numbers. That is a
# measurement index, not the content it measures, and it is what makes
# positioning work on first run. Attribution is in ATTRIBUTION.md.
!library/_vectors.json

# --- simulation output and generated reports -------------------------------
data/sim/
data/sheets/
# Gym run history: machine-local measurements, not source.
data/appgym.jsonl
data/_*.txt

# --- build inputs and generated copies -------------------------------------
# srd_raw is the input to tools/srd_convert.py. The BUILT compendium in
# app/data/compendium IS committed, so a clone works with no network.
srd_raw/
extension/app/

# --- API keys: YOURS, never ours, never committed --------------------------
# No key ships with this project. secrets.json is where you put your own, and
# it must never reach a commit. Environment variables are the alternative.
secrets.json
*.secrets.json

# --- python ----------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
*.egg-info/

# --- editors / os ----------------------------------------------------------
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
